xval/locator-power-difference/README.md gains the v2 readings of PREREGISTRATION-v2.md (signed off
9 November 2026): the session estimate per station (the mean of v1's per-epoch estimate over the
epochs it reports in), a station reporting only in more than half of the session's epochs, one
shadowing term per station (sigma_tot^2 = 6^2 + 2^2/n_i), the reference power profiled with weights
1/sigma_tot^2, tau = 1, the 10 km domain, a session with fewer than 3 reporting stations scored
against the method, the domain scope statement in every output (no detection flag), S4 read for
platforms only (Linux, macOS, Windows and debug against release; the CLI, Python and WebAssembly half
not assessable in 0.41), development seeds 3001-3200 for implementation checks only, the gate on
seeds 4001-5000 once, and oracle.py in a v2 mode. The v1 readings and results are unchanged.
